A.practical=dict(graph='Put oscillation count horizontally and elapsed time vertically. Plot the six points and a straight fitted line through their trend; these idealised values give a zero intercept.',unit='s per oscillation',meaning='The gradient estimates the period because it is elapsed time divided by the number of complete oscillations.',method=['Suspend a small bob from a fixed-length string and mark a consistent reference point for counting.','Release it from the same small angle without pushing, keeping the length unchanged.','Time a chosen number of complete oscillations using a stopwatch, counting a return to the same position and direction as one cycle.','Repeat the timing at that count and calculate a mean, investigating any anomalous reading.','Repeat for several oscillation counts while retaining the same pendulum and release conditions.'],control='Keep string length and release angle fixed. Count consistently at the same reference; keep the swinging bob clear of people.',table='Record oscillation count, each elapsed time / s and the mean elapsed time / s in separate labelled columns.',conclusion='Plot mean elapsed time against oscillation count. A straight trend with a near-zero intercept supports a constant time per cycle; obtain that time from the gradient.')
